{
  "_label": "SYNTHETIC CASES authored for plan kensaku-v1-2 (EV-018). Offer snapshots are invented but shaped like real Kensaku offers; no case comes from a live Stripe or Exa response. Frozen at approval.",
  "rules": {
    "offerId": "Lowercase hex SHA-256 of the UTF-8 string canonicalUrl + '\\n' + price.currency + '\\n' + String(price.amount) + '\\n' + exaRequestId + '\\n' + retrievedAt. Because the price is part of the id, a registered snapshot can never change price.",
    "minorUnits": "USD and SGD: amount * 100, which must be within 1e-6 of an integer; the result is that integer. JPY: the amount must be an integer and is used as is (zero-decimal). Any other currency, a non-finite amount, or an amount <= 0 is invalid.",
    "minimum": "A unit amount below the Stripe minimum (USD 50 minor units, SGD 50 minor units, JPY 50) cannot be added: below-minimum.",
    "maximum": "The cart total in minor units (sum of unit minor amount * quantity) may not exceed 99999999: total-too-large. The operation that would exceed it fails and leaves the cart unchanged.",
    "eligibility": "add takes only { offerId, quantity?, replace? }. Any other field (for example price, currency, amount) fails the strict request schema: invalid-request. An offerId with no registry entry: offer-not-registered. A registered offer with availability out_of_stock: out-of-stock. A registered offer whose price fails rules.minorUnits: invalid-price. in_stock, preorder, and unknown are addable.",
    "currency": "The cart holds one currency (null when empty). Without replace (or replace: false), adding an offer in another currency fails with currency-mismatch and reports { cartCurrency, offerCurrency }; the cart is unchanged. With replace: true, whatever the currencies, the add is evaluated against an empty cart (every check, including quantity-limit, line-limit, and total-too-large, applies to that empty cart); if it succeeds the cart holds only the new line, and if it fails the original cart is unchanged.",
    "quantity": "quantity is an integer from 1 to 10 (default 1); otherwise quantity-out-of-range. Adding an offer already in the cart adds to its quantity; a result above 10 fails with quantity-limit and leaves the line unchanged. setQuantity sets the exact value (1-10) for a line in the cart; a line not in the cart: not-in-cart. remove deletes a line; not-in-cart if absent. clear empties the cart and sets currency to null.",
    "lines": "At most 20 distinct lines. Adding a 21st distinct offer fails with line-limit.",
    "snapshot": "Each line stores demoUnitAmountMinor (from minorUnits of the registered price) and observed { amount, currency, retrievedAt, merchantHost } copied from the registry at add time. Nothing in the cart is ever read from the browser except offerId and quantity.",
    "errorPrecedence": "add: invalid-request, quantity-out-of-range, offer-not-registered, out-of-stock, invalid-price, below-minimum, currency-mismatch, quantity-limit, line-limit, total-too-large. setQuantity: invalid-request, quantity-out-of-range, not-in-cart, total-too-large. remove: invalid-request, not-in-cart. clear never fails. The first that applies is reported. An offerId that is not in the cart is not-in-cart for setQuantity and remove whether or not it is registered.",
    "generatedOffers": "A case with startGenerated seeds the cart with count distinct registered offers: canonicalUrl https://gen.example.com/p/<n> for n = 1..count, price { amount, currency } as given, exaRequestId req_gen, retrievedAt 2026-11-23T00:00:00.000Z, availability in_stock, merchantHost gen.example.com, quantity 1 each.",
    "version": "Cart.version increments by exactly 1 on every operation that succeeds and changes the cart's lines or quantities (including a replace). A failed operation, clear on an empty cart, and setQuantity to the current quantity leave the version unchanged. The webhook cart-clear rule compares this version.",
    "duplicates": "offerId includes exaRequestId and retrievedAt, so the same URL and price seen in two runs are two distinct offers and can form two cart lines. This is accepted."
  },
